    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "association": "NONE",
      "at": "2026-10-04T16:49:45Z",
      "excerpt": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **A second cancellation drops state** When a superseded handler is cancelled again during shutdown while this Redis write is awaiting I/O, the second cancellation can interrupt the write. The lock context then exits without ensuring the save completes, so state changes already yielded to the client can be lost."
